  {
   "id": "note",
   "type": "Note",
   "params": {
    "text": "Live booleans: glass and light\n\nA glowing ring sunk in a glass disc, both pierced by three spheres that orbit the axis: two Subtracts fed by the same rotating group.\n\nTurn on Live and press ▶ on the Giro slider (or drag it). While the angle moves, the Rotate → Subtract chain is redone IN THE BROWSER on meshes (manifold-wasm): no run, no round trip. The exact build123d result lands once, when it stops.\n\nThree spheres 120° apart, so 0 → 120° is a seamless loop.\n\nWhat can be anticipated: Box, Cylinder, Sphere, Move, Rotate, Union, Subtract, Intersect and value nodes wired into their pins. Any other node upstream is fine as a fixed operand (the Torus here); in the moving chain it falls back to a normal re-run."
   },
